@startuml block_size_delay
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam ArrowFontColor #e6edf7
title Transport delay per block size at 16 kHz with the same 9 ms lateness (axis in ms; project calculation)
concise "32 frames, 2 ms blocks\n1.5 ms processing budget" as small
concise "64 frames, 4 ms blocks (chosen)\n3 ms processing budget" as chosen
concise "128 frames, 8 ms blocks\n6 ms processing budget" as large
scale 4 as 70 pixels
@0
small is "7 primed × 2 ms = 14 ms"
chosen is "4 primed × 4 ms = 16 ms"
large is "3 primed × 8 ms = 24 ms"
@14
small is {-}
@16
chosen is {-}
@24
large is {-}
@32
highlight 29.8 to 30.2 #f08a7c : P03 target 30 ms
legend bottom
  Block period = frames ÷ 16,000 Hz. Processing budget = 3/4 of the block period (P02).
  Primed TX blocks n: smallest n with (n − 1) × block period − processing budget ≥ 9 ms, the lateness the chosen 64-frame design allows.
  Transport delay = n × block period. Converter filter delays (about 2.3 ms) come on top and are equal for all three.
  32 frames: 2 ms less delay, but 1.5 ms per block for processing and twice the thread wake-ups. 128 frames: 8 ms more delay.
endlegend
@enduml
